The move drill's hold at a hand-over's step (apps/mbui/e2e/move.ts, part 9m), for a COPY of the tree the drill
builds, never the product: nothing of it is committed under station/. Applied with `git apply` to a checkout of main
from before the fix of 2026-11-16 (move-two-processes: one process at a time acts on a hand-over), that copy's station
built (`pnpm run build` in its station/), the drill is run with
  E2E_MOVE_LIMBO_DIST=<that copy>/station/dist   the build A is handed to while the limbo is made
  E2E_DRILL_HOLD=counts:<path>                    where the hold's files go (<path>.arm, .held, .go)
and the harness gives the stations STILLFAIL_DRILL_HOLD from it (scripts/e2e-local.sh's env file). With <path>.arm
there, the next hand-over to reach `counts` (B answered its counts, before it writes gone) holds that process's main
thread until <path>.go is there, having written <path>.held; 9m makes the real run's limbo so on real processes.

